1 NOTE <p>Title: Ireland, Census, 1901, Co.Derry, Templemore, Londonderry (FHL# 0819485) </p><p><p>Publication: FHL# 0819485</p></p><p><p>Repository:</p></p><p><p>Call Number:</p></p><p><p>Media: Microfilm</
2 CONC p></p><p><p>Page: p50:22</p></p><p><p>Text: North Ward, 39 Creggan Rd, Johnston, Anthony head, Roman Catholic, age 41, inspector of postman, born in Londonderry City</p></p><p><p> Anthony was illitera
2 CONC te until his wife taught him to read and write.  He went on to teach himself Irish and learned how to bind books.  His uncle William was a bookbinder.</p></p><p><p> He had poetry published in "Young I
2 CONC reland" the precursor of the "Irish Independent" and he bound and decorated volumes of it himself.</p></p><p><p> He retired from the PostOffice at age 45, due to ill-health.</p></p><p><p> He dabbled i
2 CONC n stocks and shares and in the porperty market.  He left:</p></p><p><p>55 Creggan Road (the family home) to his daughter Elinor Sweeny, nee Johnston.</p></p><p><p>1 Epworth Street to his daughter Magg
2 CONC ie Gill</p></p><p><p>a property in Park Avenue to his son Anthony</p></p><p><p>BIRT: RIN MH:IF754</p></p><p><p>DEAT: RIN MH:IF755</p></p><p><p>CHR: RIN MH:IF756</p></p><p><p>RETI: RIN MH:IF758</p><p><
