1 NOTE He was the proprietor of Locust Summit Hotel, Locust Gap. [1]  He was educated in the public schools, and at the age of nine years began work in a coal breaker He was engaged at the mines until twenty
2 CONC -one years old, when he established his present business at Locust Gap in which he has been quite successful. April 14, 1887, he married Margaret, daughter of Simon and Mary (Casey) Brown, of Danville
2 CONC , Pennsylvania, and to this union has been born one daughter, Jane. Mr. Kellagher is a Catholic in faith, a Democrat in politics, and has filled the offices of school director and of county commission
2 CONC er; the latter office he filled for two successive terms, being first elected in 1881. [1]  By 1900, Michael had 6 children, 4 of whom were still alive. [2]  =Sources=  [1] https://www.findagrave.com/
2 CONC memorial/137098594/michael-j-kellagher  [2] https://freepages.rootsweb.com/~cullather/genealogy/FAMTREE/index.htm?ssmain=p1873.htm;
